       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Higher doses add substantially more adverse effects, such as peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, without much added blood pressure lowering.\n\nIs the 20 mg dose intentional, or did you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, which is the max standard dose.\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, which is the usual starting dose. Some patients, such as older or frail ones, start at 2.5 mg.\n- **A second agent added to amlodipine 10 mg**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if blood pressure still isn't controlled.\n\nIf you do want 20 mg, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's above the labeled maximum and was ordered intentionally. If you'd rather change the dose, give me the dose and I'll enter it."
      }
